BCP740- Mann Lake. Elevation 628.967 m AT GROUND LEVEL ON THE HIGHEST HILL 4.6 M N OF FENCE; 1.5 M S OF EMBANKMENT</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="697315991">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-06-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP740 Mann Lake

Posted: N54° 09.663' W111° 29.578'

MyGPSr: N54° 09.663' W111° 29.578'

(FOUND)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After parking off the road and sparking up the 4-ways, I made my way up to the top of the ditch to find an obvious stake, a bunch of flagging tape, but no cap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Okay, cap, if that's the way you're going to be...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I returned to the car, gathered &quot;the tools&quot; and made my way back up the incline. After firing up the metal detector I found the cap in all of 5 seconds under a layer of dirt and moss. I guess the threat of all those tools is all it took.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
